    <h2>Personal study</h2>
    <p>
      You may use public Cert Happens pages for personal study and evaluation. You may
      save or print pages for your own notes, create bookmarks, and use ordinary
      browser or accessibility features.
    </p>

    <h2>Linking and brief quotations</h2>
    <p>
      You may link to public pages and quote brief portions with clear attribution and
      a link to the original CertHappens.com page. Sharing a link is preferred when a
      complete guide, reference, or practice resource would otherwise be copied.
    </p>

    <h2>Republishing and mirroring</h2>
    <p>
      Without written permission, you may not copy, mirror, scrape for republication,
      or host substantial portions of the website or repository. This includes the
      question banks, guide collections, layouts, source code, structured data, and
      coordinated presentation of the site.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may not present copied Cert Happens material under another domain or brand,
      place it behind advertising or subscriptions, or operate it as another study
      service. Ordinary search-engine indexing and normal browser caching are not the
      kind of automated collection addressed by this restriction.
    </p>

    <h2>Public source repository</h2>
    <p>
      The source repository is public for transparency, review, and collaboration.
      Public visibility does not grant a general license to reproduce, publish,
      distribute, sublicense, sell, or operate a copy of the project. The repository
      contains a separate copyright notice with additional detail.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party material</h2>
    <p>
      Cert Happens does not claim ownership of certification names, trademarks,
      official exam objectives, standards, factual concepts, or third-party software.
      Those materials remain subject to their respective owners and licenses. Cert
      Happens claims rights only in original material and protectable selection,
